    <!-- Chapter 3 -->
    <section id="ch3">
      <h2>3. Heritability Estimation: From Twins to Genomic REML (GREML)</h2>

      <h3>Falconer's Twin Formula</h3>
      <p>
        Classic quantitative genetics estimates heritability by comparing phenotypic correlations between Monozygotic twins (<Katex tex="r_{\text{MZ}}" />, sharing 100% of their DNA) and Dizygotic twins (<Katex tex="r_{\text{DZ}}" />, sharing on average 50% of segregating alleles):
      </p>

      <div class="deep-dive-equation-card">
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-header">Falconer's Heritability Formula (1960)</div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-body">
          <Katex tex="r_{\text{MZ}} = h^2 + c^2, \quad r_{\text{DZ}} = \frac{1}{2}h^2 + c^2 \implies h^2 = 2(r_{\text{MZ}} - r_{\text{DZ}}), \quad c^2 = 2r_{\text{DZ}} - r_{\text{MZ}}" display={true} />
        </div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-legend">
          <Katex tex="c^2" /> = Variance contributed by shared environmental factors between twins.
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>The "Missing Heritability" Dilemma</h3>
      <p>
        When the first wave of GWAS arrived (2007–2010), a major crisis emerged: genome-wide significant hits (<Katex tex="P < 5 \times 10^{-8}" />) explained only a tiny fraction of twin-estimated heritability (e.g. for human height, twin <Katex tex="h^2 \approx 80\%" />, but significant GWAS loci explained only <Katex tex="\approx 5\%" />).
      </p>

      <h3>The Genomic Relatedness Matrix (GRM) & GCTA</h3>
      <p>
        In a breakthrough paper, <strong>Yang et al. (2010) (GCTA)</strong> resolved this dilemma by demonstrating that the "missing" heritability was not absent—it was scattered across hundreds of thousands of common SNPs with effect sizes too small to achieve genome-wide significance individually.
      </p>
      <p>
        Yang et al. constructed the <strong>Genomic Relatedness Matrix (GRM)</strong> <Katex tex="\mathbf{A}" /> from <Katex tex="M" /> genotyped SNPs across <Katex tex="N" /> unrelated individuals:
      </p>

      <div class="deep-dive-equation-card">
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-header">Yang et al. (2010) / VanRaden (2008) Genomic Relatedness Estimator</div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-body">
          <Katex tex="A_{ik} = \frac{1}{M} \sum_{j=1}^{M} \frac{(X_{ij} - 2p_j)(X_{kj} - 2p_j)}{2p_j (1 - p_j)} \implies \mathbf{A} = \frac{\mathbf{W}\mathbf{W}^T}{M}" display={true} />
        </div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-legend">
          <Katex tex="X_{ij} \in \{0, 1, 2\}" /> = Genotype dosage of individual <Katex tex="i" /> at SNP <Katex tex="j" /> &emsp;|&emsp;
          <Katex tex="p_j" /> = Sample minor allele frequency at SNP <Katex tex="j" /> &emsp;|&emsp;
          <Katex tex="W_{ij} = \frac{X_{ij} - 2p_j}{\sqrt{2p_j(1 - p_j)}}" />.
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Genomic-REML (GREML) & Liability-Scale Transformation</h3>
      <p>
        GCTA fits a linear mixed model with random polygenic effects via Restricted Maximum Likelihood (REML):
      </p>

      <div class="deep-dive-equation-card">
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-header">GREML Linear Mixed Model & Lee et al. (2011) Liability Scale Conversion</div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-body">
          <Katex tex="\mathbf{y} = \mathbf{X}\boldsymbol{\beta} + \mathbf{g} + \boldsymbol{\epsilon}, \quad \mathbf{g} \sim \mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0}, \sigma_g^2 \mathbf{A}), \quad \mathbf{V} = \sigma_g^2 \mathbf{A} + \sigma_e^2 \mathbf{I}, \qquad h^2_l = h^2_o \frac{K^2(1 - K)^2}{z_K^2 P(1 - P)}" display={true} />
        </div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-legend">
          <Katex tex="h^2_o = \frac{\sigma_g^2}{\sigma_g^2 + \sigma_e^2}" /> = Observed scale heritability in case-control study &emsp;|&emsp;
          <Katex tex="K" /> = Population disease prevalence &emsp;|&emsp;
          <Katex tex="P" /> = Sample proportion of cases &emsp;|&emsp;
          <Katex tex="z_K = \phi(\Phi^{-1}(1 - K))" /> = Standard normal height at disease threshold.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="algo-promo-card" style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
        <h3>📖 Dedicated Deep Dive: Heritability Estimation & GREML (GCTA)</h3>
        <p>
