          <span>Read Full Deep Dive on GREML & Heritability</span>
          <Icon name="arrow-right" size={15} />
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Chapter 4 -->
    <section id="ch4">
      <h2>4. Summary-Statistics Heritability: LD Score Regression (LDSC & S-LDSC)</h2>
      <p>
        GREML requires individual-level genotype matrices (<Katex tex="\mathcal{O}(N^2)" /> memory), making it computationally intractable and ethically restricted for millions of biobank participants. <strong>LD Score Regression (LDSC, Bulik-Sullivan et al. 2015)</strong> estimates <Katex tex="h^2" /> directly from public GWAS summary statistics.
      </p>

      <h3>Defining the LD Score</h3>
      <div class="deep-dive-equation-card">
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-header">Single-Variant LD Score</div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-body">
          <Katex tex="\ell_j = \sum_{k=1}^{M} r_{jk}^2" display={true} />
        </div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-legend">
          Sums the squared correlation of variant <Katex tex="j" /> with all other <Katex tex="M" /> variants in the genome (precomputed from reference panels like 1000 Genomes).
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>The Fundamental LDSC Theorem & Mathematical Proof</h3>
      <div class="deep-dive-equation-card">
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-header">Bulik-Sullivan et al. (2015) Fundamental LDSC Expectation</div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-body">
          <Katex tex="\mathbb{E}[\chi^2_j] = 1 + N a + \frac{N h^2}{M} \ell_j" display={true} />
        </div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-legend">
          <Katex tex="\chi^2_j = z_j^2" /> = GWAS chi-squared association statistic &emsp;|&emsp;
          Slope = <Katex tex="\frac{N h^2}{M}" /> (estimates SNP heritability) &emsp;|&emsp;
          Intercept = <Katex tex="1 + Na" /> (measures confounding from population stratification and cryptic relatedness).
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Cross-Trait Genetic Correlation (r_g)</h3>
      <div class="deep-dive-equation-card">
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-header">Bivariate Cross-Trait LD Score Regression</div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-body">
          <Katex tex="\mathbb{E}[z_{1j} z_{2j}] = \frac{\rho_0 N_s}{\sqrt{N_1 N_2}} + \frac{\sqrt{N_1 N_2} \rho_g}{M} \ell_j, \qquad r_g = \frac{\rho_g}{\sqrt{h_1^2 h_2^2}}" display={true} />
        </div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-legend">
          <Katex tex="z_{1j}, z_{2j}" /> = Z-scores for trait 1 and trait 2 &emsp;|&emsp;
          <Katex tex="ho_g" /> = Genetic covariance &emsp;|&emsp;
          <Katex tex="N_s" /> = Sample overlap count &emsp;|&emsp;
          <Katex tex="\rho_0" /> = Phenotypic correlation among shared samples.
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Stratified LDSC (S-LDSC, Finucane et al. 2015)</h3>
      <p>
        Partitions the genome into <Katex tex="C" /> overlapping functional annotations (e.g. cell-type-specific H3K27ac enhancers, conserved regions, coding exons):
      </p>

      <div class="deep-dive-equation-card">
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-header">Stratified LDSC Model, Enrichment & Standardized Effect (τ*)</div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-body">
          <Katex tex="\mathbb{E}[\chi^2_j] = 1 + N a + N \sum_{c=1}^{C} \tau_c \ell(j, c), \qquad \text{Enrichment}(c) = \frac{h^2(c) / h^2_{\text{total}}}{|c| / M}, \qquad \tau_c^* = \frac{M \tau_c \operatorname{sd}(c)}{h^2_{\text{total}}}" display={true} />
        </div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-legend">
          <Katex tex="\ell(j, c) = \sum_{k \in c} r_{jk}^2" /> = Stratified LD score with respect to category <Katex tex="c" /> &emsp;|&emsp;
          <Katex tex="\tau_c" /> = Raw per-SNP heritability contribution &emsp;|&emsp;
          <Katex tex="\tau_c^*" /> = Standardized conditional effect size per standard deviation of annotation (Gazal et al. 2017).
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="algo-promo-card" style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
        <h3>📖 Dedicated Deep Dive: Summary Heritability via LDSC & Stratified LDSC</h3>
        <p>
          Step-by-step mathematical proof of the Bulik-Sullivan et al. (2015) fundamental LDSC expectation, intercept diagnostics for population confounding, cross-trait genetic correlation (r_g), and functional partitioning with S-LDSC.
        </p>
