          <span>Read Full Deep Dive on LD Score Regression</span>
          <Icon name="arrow-right" size={15} />
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Chapter 5 -->
    <section id="ch5">
      <h2>5. Association Testing, Confounding & Linear Mixed Models (LMM)</h2>

      <h3>Marginal Testing & Statistical Power</h3>
      <p>
        For quantitative traits, single-marker Ordinary Least Squares (OLS) tests <Katex tex="H_0: \beta_j = 0" />:
      </p>

      <div class="deep-dive-equation-card">
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-header">OLS Marginal Regression & Non-Central Chi-Square Power</div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-body">
          <Katex tex="\hat{\beta}_j = \frac{\mathbf{x}_j^T \mathbf{y}}{\mathbf{x}_j^T \mathbf{x}_j}, \quad z_j = \frac{\hat{\beta}_j}{\text{SE}(\hat{\beta}_j)}, \qquad \lambda = \frac{2N p(1 - p)\beta^2}{\sigma^2} \implies \chi^2_1 \sim \chi^2_1(\lambda)" display={true} />
        </div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-legend">
          <Katex tex="\lambda" /> = Noncentrality parameter (NCP). At genome-wide significance <Katex tex="\alpha = 5 \times 10^{-8}" /> (<Katex tex="z_{\alpha/2} \approx 5.451" />), achieving 80% statistical power requires <Katex tex="\lambda \ge (5.451 + 0.842)^2 \approx 39.6" />.
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Confounding Structures & Genomic Inflation (λ_GC)</h3>
      <div class="deep-dive-equation-card">
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-header">Genomic Inflation Factor</div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-body">
          <Katex tex="\lambda_{\text{GC}} = \frac{\text{median}(\chi^2_1, \chi^2_2, \dots, \chi^2_M)}{0.454936}" display={true} />
        </div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-legend">
          <Katex tex="0.454936" /> is the theoretical median of a central <Katex tex="\chi^2_1" /> distribution. In massive biobanks (<Katex tex="N > 100,000" />), true polygenicity inflates <Katex tex="\lambda_{\text{GC}} > 1.2" />, making LDSC intercept the definitive test for residual confounding.
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Computational Evolution of Linear Mixed Models</h3>
      <div class="paper-table-wrap">
        <table class="paper-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Method / Tool</th>
              <th>Algorithmic Breakthrough</th>
              <th>Computational Complexity</th>
              <th>Cohort Scalability</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>GEMMA / FaST-LMM (2012)</strong></td>
              <td>Spectral eigen-decomposition of GRM <Katex tex="\mathbf{A} = \mathbf{U}\mathbf{S}\mathbf{U}^T" />.</td>
              <td><Katex tex="\mathcal{O}(N^3)" /> upfront + <Katex tex="\mathcal{O}(MN)" /> testing.</td>
              <td><Katex tex="N \le 20,000" /></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>BOLT-LMM (Loh et al. 2015)</strong></td>
              <td>Mixture-of-Gaussians spike-and-slab prior + Conjugate gradient solver without inverting <Katex tex="\mathbf{A}" />.</td>
              <td><Katex tex="\mathcal{O}(M_{\text{GRM}} N \times \text{iterations})" /></td>
              <td><Katex tex="N \approx 500,000" /> (UK Biobank scale)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>fastGWA (Jiang et al. 2019)</strong></td>
              <td>Sparse GRM thresholding (<Katex tex="A_{ik} < 0.05 \to 0" />) with Cholesky factorization.</td>
              <td>Linear in non-zero entries of sparse matrix.</td>
              <td><Katex tex="N \approx 1,000,000" /></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>REGENIE (Mbatchou et al. 2021)</strong></td>
              <td>Step 1 stacked ridge regression cross-validation; Step 2 linear regression (quantitative) or logistic score test with thresholded Firth/SPA fallback (binary).</td>
              <td>Split-block parallelization; <Katex tex="\mathcal{O}(N)" /> memory.</td>
              <td><Katex tex="N > 1,000,000" /> (Exome/WGS biobanks)</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

