    <!-- Chapter 6 -->
    <section id="ch6">
      <h2>6. Bayesian Fine-Mapping & Causal Variant Prioritization</h2>

      <h3>The Fundamental LD Confounding Equation</h3>
      <p>
        Because of Linkage Disequilibrium, the marginal GWAS effect estimates <Katex tex="\hat{\boldsymbol{\beta}}" /> are linear combinations of all true causal effects <Katex tex="\boldsymbol{\beta}_{\text{true}}" /> weighted by the LD correlation matrix <Katex tex="\mathbf{R}" />:
      </p>

      <div class="deep-dive-equation-card">
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-header">LD Confounding Matrix Equation</div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-body">
          <Katex tex="\mathbb{E}[\hat{\boldsymbol{\beta}}] = \mathbf{R} \boldsymbol{\beta}_{\text{true}}" display={true} />
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Wakefield's Approximate Bayes Factor (ABF, 2009) & Null Normalization</h3>
      <div class="deep-dive-equation-card">
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-header">Wakefield ABF Formulation & Null-Inclusive PIP</div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-body">
          <Katex tex="\text{ABF}_j = \sqrt{\frac{V_j + W}{V_j}} \exp\left(-\frac{z_j^2}{2} \frac{W}{V_j + W}\right), \qquad \text{PIP}_j = P(\gamma_j = 1 \mid \mathcal{D}) = \frac{\pi_j / \text{ABF}_j}{\pi_0 + \sum_{k=1}^M \pi_k / \text{ABF}_k}" display={true} />
        </div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-legend">
          <Katex tex="V_j = \text{SE}(\hat{\beta}_j)^2" /> = Measurement error variance &emsp;|&emsp;
          <Katex tex="W" /> = Prior variance of true effect sizes &emsp;|&emsp;
          <Katex tex="\pi_0" /> = Prior probability that no variant in the locus is causal.
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Sum of Single Effects (SuSiE, Wang et al. 2020)</h3>
      <p>
        SuSiE formulates fine-mapping as a sum of <Katex tex="L" /> single-effect linear regressions:
      </p>

      <div class="deep-dive-equation-card">
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-header">SuSiE Generative Model & Credible Sets</div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-body">
          <Katex tex="\mathbf{y} = \sum_{l=1}^{L} \mathbf{X} \boldsymbol{\gamma}_l b_l + \boldsymbol{\epsilon}, \quad \boldsymbol{\gamma}_l \sim \text{Multinomial}(1, \boldsymbol{\pi}), \quad b_l \sim \mathcal{N}(0, \sigma_l^2), \quad \text{Purity}(\text{CS}_l) = \min_{j, k \in \text{CS}_l} |r_{jk}| \ge 0.5" display={true} />
        </div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-legend">
          SuSiE fits this model via <strong>Iterative Bayesian Stepwise Selection (IBSS)</strong>, a coordinate ascent variational inference algorithm that optimizes the Evidence Lower Bound (ELBO) to produce calibrated 95% Credible Sets (CS).
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="algo-promo-card" style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
        <h3>📖 Dedicated Deep Dive: Bayesian Fine-Mapping & Causal Prioritization (SuSiE)</h3>
        <p>
          Master the LD confounding matrix equation, Wakefield's Approximate Bayes Factor (ABF), the Sum of Single Effects (SuSiE) model, coordinate ascent variational inference (IBSS), and empirical priors from PolyFun.
        </p>
