    <!-- Chapter 7 -->
    <section id="ch7">
      <h2>7. Rare Variant Association Testing (RVAT)</h2>

      <h3>The Single-Variant Power Cliff</h3>
      <p>
        For rare variants (<Katex tex="\text{MAF} < 0.1\%" />), statistical power in single-marker tests collapses. Under a standardized phenotype with <Katex tex="N = 100,000" /> and <Katex tex="\text{MAF} = 10^{-4}" />, achieving 80% power at <Katex tex="\alpha = 5 \times 10^{-8}" /> requires an effect magnitude <Katex tex="|\beta| \approx 1.41\text{ SD}" />, necessitating gene-level collapsing tests.
      </p>

      <h3>Gene-Level Aggregation Tests</h3>
      <div class="paper-table-wrap">
        <table class="paper-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Test Type</th>
              <th>Mathematical Formulation</th>
              <th>Key Underlying Assumption</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Burden Tests (CAST / CMC)</strong></td>
              <td><Katex tex="T_{\text{Burden}} = \left(\sum_{j=1}^m w_j \mathbf{G}_j^T (\mathbf{y} - \bar{y})\right)^2" /></td>
              <td>Assumes <strong>all rare variants act in the same direction</strong>; suffers devastating power loss if protective and risk alleles cancel out.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>SKAT (Wu et al. 2011)</strong></td>
              <td><Katex tex="\mathcal{Q}_{\text{SKAT}} = (\mathbf{y} - \hat{\boldsymbol{\mu}})^T \mathbf{K} (\mathbf{y} - \hat{\boldsymbol{\mu}}) = \sum_{j=1}^m w_j^2 S_j^2" /></td>
              <td>Variance-component score test; robust when variants have <strong>mixed directional effects or non-causal noise</strong>.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>SKAT-O (Lee et al. 2012)</strong></td>
              <td><Katex tex="\mathcal{Q}_\rho = \rho \mathcal{Q}_{\text{Burden}} + (1 - \rho)\mathcal{Q}_{\text{SKAT}}" /></td>
              <td>Data-adaptive optimal convex combination searching over <Katex tex="\rho \in [0, 1]" />.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>DeepRVAT (Karczewski et al. 2024)</strong></td>
              <td>Neural aggregation using AlphaMissense, CADD, SpliceAI, and AbSplice embeddings.</td>
              <td>Replaces heuristic MAF weights with calibrated functional deleteriousness embeddings in UK Biobank (161k quantitative / 469k binary).</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
