      <h3>Additive PRS Model</h3>
      <div class="deep-dive-equation-card">
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-header">Linear Polygenic Risk Score</div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-body">
          <Katex tex="\text{PRS}_i = \sum_{j=1}^{M} w_j G_{ij}" display={true} />
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Methodological Comparison for Deriving Weights</h3>
      <div class="paper-table-wrap">
        <table class="paper-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Method</th>
              <th>Algorithm / Prior</th>
              <th>Key Strengths & Properties</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Clumping & Thresholding (C+T)</strong></td>
              <td>Heuristic LD pruning (<Katex tex="r^2 < 0.1" />) + P-value cutoff grid search (<Katex tex="P < P_T" />).</td>
              <td>Fast and simple; discards correlated causal variants in LD.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>LDpred2 (Privé et al. 2020)</strong></td>
              <td>Bayesian Spike-and-Slab prior: <Katex tex="\beta_j \sim \pi \mathcal{N}(0, \frac{h^2}{M\pi}) + (1-\pi)\delta_0" />.</td>
              <td>Models LD correlation matrix directly via Gibbs sampling across European cohorts.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>PRS-CS (Ge et al. 2019)</strong></td>
              <td>Continuous shrinkage: <Katex tex="\beta_j \sim \mathcal{N}(0, \frac{\sigma^2}{N}\phi \psi_j), \psi_j \sim \mathcal{G}(a, \delta_j), \delta_j \sim \mathcal{G}(b, 1)" />.</td>
              <td>Robust adaptive shrinkage; PRS-CS-auto learns global parameter <Katex tex="\phi" /> using Half-Cauchy hyperprior.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>PRS-CSx (Ruan et al. 2022)</strong></td>
              <td>Multi-ancestry continuous shrinkage with population-specific LD panels.</td>
              <td>Significantly improves cross-ancestry prediction in non-European target populations.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
