    <section id="ch9">
      <h2>9. Causal Inference: Mendelian Randomization (MR)</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Mendelian Randomization (MR)</strong> uses genetic variants as <strong>Instrumental Variables (IVs)</strong> to evaluate whether an observational exposure <Katex tex="X" /> causally influences a health outcome <Katex tex="Y" /> under explicit structural assumptions.
      </p>

      <h3>The Three Core Instrumental Variable (IV) Assumptions</h3>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>1. Relevance Assumption:</strong> The genetic variant <Katex tex="Z" /> must be robustly associated with the exposure <Katex tex="X" /> (first-stage <Katex tex="F\text{-statistic} = \hat{\gamma}^2 / \text{SE}(\hat{\gamma})^2 > 10" />).</li>
        <li><strong>2. Independence Assumption:</strong> The variant <Katex tex="Z" /> is independent of all unmeasured confounders <Katex tex="U" /> between exposure and outcome (<Katex tex="Z \perp U" />).</li>
        <li><strong>3. Exclusion Restriction:</strong> The variant <Katex tex="Z" /> affects outcome <Katex tex="Y" /> <strong>strictly through exposure <Katex tex="X" /></strong> (no direct horizontal pleiotropic path <Katex tex="Z \to Y" />).</li>
      </ol>

      <h3>The Inverse-Variance Weighted (IVW) Estimator</h3>
      <div class="deep-dive-equation-card">
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-header">Single-Instrument Wald Ratio & Multi-Instrument IVW Estimator</div>
        <div class="deep-dive-equation-body">
          <Katex tex="\hat{\beta}_{\text{Wald}, j} = \frac{\hat{\Gamma}_j}{\hat{\gamma}_j}, \qquad \hat{\beta}_{\text{IVW}} = \frac{\sum_{j=1}^{K} w_j \hat{\beta}_{\text{Wald}, j}}{\sum_{j=1}^{K} w_j}, \quad w_j \approx \frac{\hat{\gamma}_j^2}{\operatorname{Var}(\hat{\Gamma}_j)}" display={true} />
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Robust Sensitivity Methods for Pleiotropy</h3>
      <div class="paper-table-wrap">
        <table class="paper-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Method</th>
              <th>Mathematical Formulation</th>
              <th>Robustness Mechanism</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>MR-Egger Regression (Bowden 2015)</strong></td>
              <td><Katex tex="\hat{\Gamma}_j = \beta_0 + \beta_{\text{Egger}} \hat{\gamma}_j + \epsilon_j" /></td>
              <td>Intercept <Katex tex="\beta_0 \neq 0" /> tests for directional horizontal pleiotropy under the InSIDE assumption.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Weighted Median (Bowden 2016)</strong></td>
              <td>Median of sorted ratio estimates <Katex tex="\hat{\beta}_{\text{Wald}, j}" /> with normalized weights.</td>
              <td>Consistent even if up to <strong>50% of the genetic weight comes from invalid instruments</strong>.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Within-Family / Sibling MR</strong></td>
              <td>Conditioning on parental genotypes or sibling difference models.</td>
              <td>Completely eliminates population stratification, assortative mating, and dynastic parental nurture.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

